                      (    forth6809.asm):02666                  ; STATE=-1, which compiles (and for immediate words, executes)
                      (    forth6809.asm):02667                  ; instead of interpreting - explaining the observed cascade
                      (    forth6809.asm):02668                  ; where one failed definition (GI5) turned every subsequent,
                      (    forth6809.asm):02669                  ; otherwise-correct test on later lines into further -13/-22
                      (    forth6809.asm):02670                  ; errors. QUIT/ABORT already reset STATE correctly (see the
                      (    forth6809.asm):02671                  ; BUG FIX comment above at this routine's entry) for a cold
                      (    forth6809.asm):02672                  ; boot or a fully-unwound ABORT; this is the matching reset
                      (    forth6809.asm):02673                  ; for QLOOP's own, lighter-weight per-line catch, which is
                      (    forth6809.asm):02674                  ; the path every ordinary typed/sent-line error actually
                      (    forth6809.asm):02675                  ; takes and previously left STATE untouched. ANS QUIT's own
                      (    forth6809.asm):02676                  ; semantics call for returning to interpretation state after
                      (    forth6809.asm):02677                  ; any uncaught exception, which is exactly this case.
