                      (    forth6809.asm):04625                                   ; EXIT's own EXITUNLOOP mechanism already
                      (    forth6809.asm):04626                                   ; discards the frame automatically and
                      (    forth6809.asm):04627                                   ; correctly on every path - traced and
                      (    forth6809.asm):04628                                   ; confirmed: with no enclosing DO (compiled
                      (    forth6809.asm):04629                                   ; count 0), with one enclosing DO and no
                      (    forth6809.asm):04630                                   ; prior UNLOOP (discards the full 8-byte
                      (    forth6809.asm):04631                                   ; frame correctly). The one combination that
                      (    forth6809.asm):04632                                   ; broke was UNLOOP immediately before EXIT -
                      (    forth6809.asm):04633                                   ; UNLOOP discarding 6 of the 8 bytes itself,
                      (    forth6809.asm):04634                                   ; then EXITUNLOOP unconditionally discarding
                      (    forth6809.asm):04635                                   ; a full 8 more, overshooting into whatever
                      (    forth6809.asm):04636                                   ; sat below (typically the caller's own
                      (    forth6809.asm):04637                                   ; return address) and branching into random
                      (    forth6809.asm):04638                                   ; memory on return. Since UNLOOP has no
                      (    forth6809.asm):04639                                   ; other legitimate use than immediately
                      (    forth6809.asm):04640                                   ; preceding an exit from the definition, and
                      (    forth6809.asm):04641                                   ; EXIT already handles that correctly on its
                      (    forth6809.asm):04642                                   ; own, UNLOOP is now a true no-op rather than
