                      (    forth6809.asm):05811                                  ; unrelated, earlier instruction happened to
                      (    forth6809.asm):05812                                  ; leave set, not the sign of the value just
                      (    forth6809.asm):05813                                  ; popped. TSTA explicitly tests D's high byte
                      (    forth6809.asm):05814                                  ; (bit 7 of A reflects the full 16-bit value's
                      (    forth6809.asm):05815                                  ; sign) immediately before the branch that
                      (    forth6809.asm):05816                                  ; depends on it. Confirmed via MAME debugger:
