                      (    forth6809.asm):07082                                  ; after PULU - PULU doesn't affect condition
                      (    forth6809.asm):07083                                  ; codes on genuine 6809 (same class as STOD's
                      (    forth6809.asm):07084                                  ; own fix elsewhere in this file), so BPL was
                      (    forth6809.asm):07085                                  ; testing whatever flags an unrelated, earlier
                      (    forth6809.asm):07086                                  ; instruction happened to leave set, not the
                      (    forth6809.asm):07087                                  ; sign of the value just popped. TSTA
                      (    forth6809.asm):07088                                  ; explicitly tests D's high byte immediately
                      (    forth6809.asm):07089                                  ; before the branch that depends on it. The
                      (    forth6809.asm):07090                                  ; four existing internal callers (DOT/DOTR/
                      (    forth6809.asm):07091                                  ; DDOT/DDOTR, i.e. . / .R / D. / D.R) were
                      (    forth6809.asm):07092                                  ; accidentally unaffected - each happens to
                      (    forth6809.asm):07093                                  ; run "LDD SAVEN" (a flag-setting load of the
                      (    forth6809.asm):07094                                  ; true signed value) immediately before PSHU
                      (    forth6809.asm):07095                                  ; D/JSR SIGN, and PSHU doesn't disturb flags -
                      (    forth6809.asm):07096                                  ; but this was fragile, caller-side luck, not
                      (    forth6809.asm):07097                                  ; SIGN being correct on its own. Confirmed via
                      (    forth6809.asm):07098                                  ; MAME: a direct, standalone use of SIGN (not
                      (    forth6809.asm):07099                                  ; preceded by an unrelated flag-setting
                      (    forth6809.asm):07100                                  ; instruction) never added the minus sign for
                      (    forth6809.asm):07101                                  ; either sign of input.
